0 HEAD
1 SOUR MYHERITAGE
2 NAME MyHeritage Family Tree Builder
2 VERS 8.0
2 CORP MyHeritage.com
1 GEDC
2 VERS 5.5.1
2 FORM LINEAGE-LINKED
1 CHAR UTF-8
1 NOTE Notes carrying HTML, which the specification neither blesses nor forbids:
2 CONT to GEDCOM 5.5.1 a note is text, and markup in it is text like any other.
2 CONT The interesting part is CONC, which joins with no separator at all — so a
2 CONT tag split across two lines is only whole once the lines are rejoined.
0 @I1@ INDI
1 NAME Cecil John /Rhodes/
2 GIVN Cecil John
2 SURN Rhodes
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 5 JUL 1853
2 PLAC Bishop's Stortford, Hertfordshire, England
1 NOTE <p>He was an accountant for <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cons
2 CONC olidated_Gold_Fields">Consolidated Gold Fields</a>, founded in 1887.</p>
1 NOTE <p>The company register is searchable at https://find-and-update.company
2 CONC -information.service.gov.uk/advanced-search/get-results?companyNameInclud
2 CONC es=Consolidated+Gold+Fields&amp;companyNameExcludes=&amp;status=active
1 SOUR @S1@
2 QUAY 3
2 DATA
3 TEXT Added by confirming a Smart Match
2 EVEN Smart Matching
3 ROLE I500007
0 @I2@ INDI
1 NAME Alfred /Beit/
1 SEX M
1 NOTE <p>Well formed, and closed where it should be.</p>
1 NOTE <p>Unclosed, which no GEDCOM rule has anything to say about.
1 NOTE Mixed <b>bold and <i>italic</i></b> nested correctly.
1 NOTE Crossed <b>bold and <i>italic</b> here</i>, which is not well formed.
1 NOTE 5 < 7 and 7 > 5, where the angle brackets are arithmetic rather than tags.
1 NOTE An unescaped ampersand: Marks & Spencer, beside an escaped one: &amp;.
1 NOTE @@ is how 5.5.1 escapes a literal at-sign, as in user@@example.org.
0 @S1@ SOUR
1 TITL Consolidated Gold Fields of South Africa
1 NOTE <p>A source note, inline rather than pointing at a note record — which is
2 CONT the form the specification lists second and exporters write first.</p>
0 @N1@ NOTE An ordinary note record, pointed at from nowhere in particular.
1 CONT It exists so the file carries both spellings of a note.
0 TRLR
